  "answer": "Citation complaints declined steadily from Q1 to Q2. In Q1 2026, there was a sharp increase in citation error tickets, prompting a deep-dive review of 210 accuracy-related tickets [NL-010#NL-010-S05]. In Q2, after the April release, citation accuracy tickets dropped significantly—from 88 in March to 42 in April, 31 in May, and 24 in June—and the Q2 feedback report confirms citation-related complaints decreased significantly [NL-011#NL-011-S05][NL-016#NL-016-S04].\n\nThe remaining scanned-document problem (image-only PDFs that still cause citation failures) is directly addressed by the planned \"Advanced OCR Pipeline.\" Product plans include integrating a standard OCR engine into the KnowledgeHub ingestion queue and designing an Admin Console interface to show text extraction quality scores, with a target to launch the OCR pilot by August 2026 [NL-010#NL-010-S10]. This pipeline is scheduled for release in August 2026 and will automatically extract text and layout structures from scanned files to allow for page-specific citations [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
